\textbf{Why RevIN destroys routing.} Each window decomposes into mean $M_i$, scale $\Sigma_i$, shape $\mathbf{S}_i = (\mathbf{x}_i - M_i)/\Sigma_i$; RevIN keeps $\mathbf{S}_i$ and discards $(M_i,\Sigma_i)$. The chain rule quantifies the routing signal in the discarded part.

